  "[RUIN_RATO_DESC]", "This is the home of Arik, the minotaur king.";
  "[RUIN_RATO_NAME]", "Arik's Arena";
  "[RUIN_RBST_DESC]", "This rock formation marks the place where Lord Bane was once defeated by the Elven Mages.";
  "[RUIN_RBST_NAME]", "Bloodstone";
  "[RUIN_RCBL_DESC]", "The Frost Dragon, Chilblain, lives here.";
  "[RUIN_RCBL_NAME]", "Chilblain's Lair";
  "[RUIN_RDCV_DESC]", "This cave belongs to a Green Dragon who has lived within sight of Drakenburg for many centuries.";
  "[RUIN_RDCV_NAME]", "Dragon Cave";
  "[RUIN_RDGV_DESC]", "The bones of Dragons litter the ground in this silent valley.";
  "[RUIN_RDGV_NAME]", "Dragons' Graveyard";
  "[RUIN_RDPS_DESC]", "Members of the Dark Path Cult are said to worship at this shrine.";
  "[RUIN_RDPS_NAME]", "Dark Path Shrine";
  "[RUIN_RDSH_DESC]", "This is an ancient Elven shrine, originally used to worship the Frost Dragons who lived in these mountains.";
  "[RUIN_RDSH_NAME]", "Dragon Shrine";
  "[RUIN_RDST_DESC]", "Lord Bane keeps his mounts stabled in these dark uninviting caves.";
  "[RUIN_RDST_NAME]", "Dark Stables";
  "[RUIN_REGB_DESC]", "Egor the Troll lives under this Bridge.";
  "[RUIN_REGB_NAME]", "Egor's Bridge";
  "[RUIN_RGSE_DESC]", "These sewers carry away the wastes from the busy citadel of Gildor.";
  "[RUIN_RGSE_NAME]", "Gildine Sewers";
  "[RUIN_RHAG_DESC]", "The Hagstone is home to a large coven of Harpies.";
  "[RUIN_RHAG_NAME]", "Hagstone";
  "[RUIN_RICM_DESC]", "The Elves have dug deep into the Ice here, mining precious metals.";
  "[RUIN_RICM_NAME]", "Ice Crystal Mine";
  "[RUIN_RMOL_DESC]", "The Swamp Dragon, Morass, lives here.";
  "[RUIN_RMOL_NAME]", "Morass' Lair";
  "[RUIN_ROOU_DESC]", "This was once a Selentine military outpost, but Elenian archers destroyed it.";
  "[RUIN_ROOU_NAME]", "Old Outpost";
  "[RUIN_ROTO_DESC]", "Two Ogres live in this tower on the edge of the Barad Dumyr.";
  "[RUIN_ROTO_NAME]", "Ogre's Tower";
  "[RUIN_RSCC_DESC]", "Giant Scorpions inhabit this cave and terrorize any passersby.";
  "[RUIN_RSCC_NAME]", "Scorpions' Cave";
  "[RUIN_RSCV_DESC]", "An ancient Flame Dragon is said to slumber in this cave.";
  "[RUIN_RSCV_NAME]", "Swamp Cave";
  "[RUIN_RSKM_DESC]", "These marshes are home to all manner of foul and twisted creatures.";
  "[RUIN_RSKM_NAME]", "Skell Marshes";
  "[RUIN_RSLV_DESC]", "Minotaur Slavers often land here and raid southern Selentia and the Trarg.";
  "[RUIN_RSLV_NAME]", "Slaver Camp";
  "[RUIN_RSTR_DESC]", "An ancient order of Elenian Druids worship at this Grove.";
  "[RUIN_RSTR_NAME]", "Ancient Grove";
  "[RUIN_RTHC_DESC]", "The Kings of Theira are buried here.";
  "[RUIN_RTHC_NAME]", "Royal Crypt";
  "[RUIN_RTLH_DESC]", "Trolls live in this cave deep within the marsh.";
  "[RUIN_RTLH_NAME]", "Troll Hole";
  "[RUIN_RUML_DESC]", "The Flame Dragon, Umbra, lives here.";
  "[RUIN_RUML_NAME]", "Umbra's Lair";
  "[RUIN_RVOL_DESC]", "This Volcano is home to a large number of Fire Elementals.";
  "[RUIN_RVOL_NAME]", "Volcano";
  "[RUIN_RWCV_DESC]", "Giant worms live here. The Orcs of Kor highly prize them for their meat.";
  "[RUIN_RWCV_NAME]", "Worm Cave";
  "[RUIN_RWGS_DESC]", "Out west of Gruuldok, the plains are infested by Wargs.";
  "[RUIN_RWGS_NAME]", "Wargstone";
  "[RUIN_RWHV_DESC]", "Giant Wasps inhabit a hive within this cave.";
  "[RUIN_RWHV_NAME]", "Wasp Hive";
  "[RUIN_RWRO_DESC]", "A pack of Wyverns live on a peak at the end of a long, dry valley.";
  "[RUIN_RWRO_NAME]", "Wyvern's Roost";
  "[RUMORS]", "Rumors";
  "[RUMORS_DETAILS]", "%d Rumors known";
  "[RUMORS_HELP]", "Collect new Rumors at Taverns. They will give you hints about the game and story. \\n The most important rumors are marked with an exclamation point, and remain at the top of the list for longer.";
  "[RUMOR_U000_DESC]", "There are five Orders of Knights in Agaria - the Bartonians are the largest, but each of the other four Orders--Sirians, Elenians, Theirans and Gildines--is equally prestigious in their own way.";
  "[RUMOR_U000_NAME]", "Knightly Orders";
  "[RUMOR_U001_DESC]", "It is rumored that Syrus Darkhunter was once a Riverguard Knight, but was exiled from the Order after an argument with its leader, Lord Greythane.";
  "[RUMOR_U001_NAME]", "Darkhunter's History";
  "[RUMOR_U002_DESC]", "The Green Dragon who lives in the mountains north of Drakenburg has not been seen for some time.  The folk of Drakenburg are not sorry to see him go!";
  "[RUMOR_U002_NAME]", "Drakenburg's Dragon";
  "[RUMOR_U003_DESC]", "The Dwarves up in the Agarian Pass have reported seeing many Griffons, Ogres and Orcs recently. The pass is a dangerous place and they recommend keeping travel there to a minimum.";
  "[RUMOR_U003_NAME]", "Griffons";
  "[RUMOR_U004_DESC]", "The people of The Trarg are very excited about the upcoming wedding of their leader to the Imperial Princess, Serephine.";
  "[RUMOR_U004_NAME]", "Imperial Wedding";
  "[RUMOR_U005_DESC]", "Bartonia is the largest of the citadels in the Agarian Empire. Many young nobles and squires are sent here to train as part of their education.";
  "[RUMOR_U005_NAME]", "Bartonia";
  "[RUMOR_U006_DESC]", "The Palace Guard of Bartonia is a popular training academy for young nobles. There, they can learn basic magic, fighting skills and how to behave in the royal court.";
  "[RUMOR_U006_NAME]", "Palace Guard";
  "[RUMOR_U007_DESC]", "The people of the Trarg tell you that a mount moves you faster, and that a well-trained mount can help you avoid many encounters. To get a mount you should first build a Dungeon in your citadel.";
  "[RUMOR_U007_NAME]", "Mounts";
  "[RUMOR_U008_DESC]", "Once part of the mighty Lysean Empire before its fall, the Borderlands is now a region of small Duchies ruled over by numerous petty Barons and Dukes.";
  "[RUMOR_U008_NAME]", "The Borderlands";
  "[RUMOR_U009_DESC]", "The Knights of the Riverguard live in the Red Tower, inside the Citadel of Maethelburg. They patrol the river to help keep their part of the Borderlands safe.";
  "[RUMOR_U009_NAME]", "Riverguard";
  "[RUMOR_U010_DESC]", "Wood Elves are the least populous of the three Elven peoples (High Elves, Dark Elves and Wood Elves). They only have two settlements in Etheria--Silvermyr and Solhaven, which is on the Isle of Dawn.";
  "[RUMOR_U010_NAME]", "Wood Elves";
  "[RUMOR_U011_DESC]", "The Wood Elves of Silvermyr are ruled by King Oberon and Queen Titania. They have been close allies of the Agarian Knights for many centuries.";
  "[RUMOR_U011_NAME]", "Wood Elf Royalty";
  "[RUMOR_U012_DESC]", "The evil decrepit Duke of Skellheim rules this swampy land in the middle of the Borderlands. Many folks say that he is a Necromancer.";
  "[RUMOR_U012_NAME]", "Skellheim";
  "[RUMOR_U013_DESC]", "The Dwarven outpost of Dhun-Kor was established to trade with the Orcs and Goblins on the plains of Kor. Typically Dwarves hate Orcs, but if there is a profit involved they can put hatred aside.";
  "[RUMOR_U013_NAME]", "Dhun-Kor";
  "[RUMOR_U014_DESC]", "This position - leader of the Orc tribes of Kor - is chosen by combat. The title is in many ways irrelevant since it has been many centuries since a Great Orc united enough tribes to cross the mountains and do any serious damage.";
  "[RUMOR_U014_NAME]", "The Great Orc";
  "[RUMOR_U015_DESC]", "Not too long ago, Gruuldok was only a small Orcish tribal village.  It has risen to prominence since its chieftain Gruulkar became the Great Orc.";
  "[RUMOR_U015_NAME]", "Gruuldok";
  "[RUMOR_U016_DESC]", "Ogres are amongst the worst cooks in Etheria.  There is nothing an Ogre will not throw in his pot to make a meal. Some Sages believe that Ogres actually have no tastebuds at all.";
  "[RUMOR_U016_NAME]", "Ogre Cooking";
  "[RUMOR_U017_DESC]", "The Ogres are ruled by a council of Ogre Mages. These creatures are feared by many because they control a wild chaotic form of magic. Sadly, the only thing more chaotic than their magic is their form of government.";
  "[RUMOR_U017_NAME]", "Ogre Mages";
  "[RUMOR_U018_DESC]", "Many types of Dragons usually inhabit the Dragonrealm, each of them a different color. There are Flame Dragons, Frost Dragons, Swamp Dragons, and Storm Dragons.";
  "[RUMOR_U018_NAME]", "Dragons";
  "[RUMOR_U019_DESC]", "Kelthurax, the ancient Flame Dragon, is perhaps the oldest creature still alive in Etheria today. He can still remember the Sundering almost 3000 years ago, when half the world was destroyed.";
  "[RUMOR_U019_NAME]", "Kelthurax";
  "[RUMOR_U020_DESC]", "Firewalkers are Minotaur Priests, worshippers of Lord Sartek.  Since Sartek fell in battle, their power in the Realms of War has been waning.";
  "[RUMOR_U020_NAME]", "Firewalkers";
  "[RUMOR_U021_DESC]", "Lord Bane attacked his brother Lord Sartek because Lord Bane was angry when Sartek withdrew from battle against the Agarian Knights in the Banewars, 500 years ago.";
  "[RUMOR_U021_NAME]", "Sartek's Treachery";
  "[RUMOR_U022_DESC]", "Lord Sartek and Lord Bane are two of the Four Horsemen -- War and Death. Lords Antharg and Melchor -- Plague and Famine -- live far away in the south and west.";
  "[RUMOR_U022_NAME]", "The Four Horsemen";
  "[RUMOR_U023_DESC]", "Gnolls were another creature created by Lord Sartek.  He grafted a dog's head onto a Human body.  Gnolls are cunning and fast, and they attack in packs.";
  "[RUMOR_U023_NAME]", "Gnolls";
  "[RUMOR_U024_DESC]", "Just like most canine creatures, the Gnolls of Hyaan are constantly struggling for dominance.  Currently a Gnoll called Staf is trying to take over their city.";
  "[RUMOR_U024_NAME]", "Trouble in Hyaan";
  "[RUMOR_U025_DESC]", "The huge Palace of Ohtar was home to Lord Sartek for many, many centuries before Lord Bane exacted his revenge.";
  "[RUMOR_U025_NAME]", "Ohtar";
  "[RUMOR_U026_DESC]", "Ylarie was overrun many centuries ago by an Orc named Gornak Elfeater. Strangely, the High Elves never rebuilt the city.";
  "[RUMOR_U026_NAME]", "Ylarie Ruins";
  "[RUMOR_U027_DESC]", "The High Elves are ruled by two monarchs, the Ice Queen who lives in Ehlariel, and the Moon King who lives on the isle of Lunarion.";
  "[RUMOR_U027_NAME]", "High Elven Royalty";
  "[RUMOR_U028_DESC]", "Three passes exist into the Realms of Death, two of which are guarded by the High Elves.  They are called Skullguard Pass and Iceguard Pass.  The two Keeps in these passes have not fallen since the Banewars, 500 years ago.";
  "[RUMOR_U028_NAME]", "The Passes of Death";
  "[RUMOR_U029_DESC]", "Ragnar is an ancient Frost Dragon who can often be found on the coast to the west of Ehlariel.  He has lived in the nearby mountains so long that they are now known as the Mountains of Ragnar.";
  "[RUMOR_U029_NAME]", "Ragnar the Dragon";
  "[RUMOR_U030_DESC]", "Five hundred years ago, Lord Bane staged a massive invasion throughout Etheria but was finally pushed back by the Sirian Knights who defeated him.";
  "[RUMOR_U030_NAME]", "The Banewars";
  "[RUMOR_U031_DESC]", "One hundred years after he fell in the Banewars, Lord Bane rose again.  This time he made a surgically precise strike into Agaria to slay the knights who defeated him in battle.";
  "[RUMOR_U031_NAME]", "Bane's Revenge";
  "[RUMOR_U032_DESC]", "This Citadel of Lord Bane is a mass of interconnecting torture chambers and dungeons, filled with the screams of victims. Bane works tirelessly to create new Undead creatures.";
  "[RUMOR_U032_NAME]", "Lord Bane's Citadel";
  "[RUMOR_U033_DESC]", "Dark Dwarves were once members of the regular Dwarven Clans. After the Great Dwarven Plague, they set out on a long journey. Unfortunately Bane corrupted them as they passed through his lands.";
  "[RUMOR_U033_NAME]", "Dark Dwarves";
  "[RUMOR_U034_DESC]", "When the Dwarves of Khaz-Barak tunneled too near the Realms of Plague, Lord Antharg inflicted them with a terrible disease that killed nearly a third of them.  They have never fully recovered from this.";
  "[RUMOR_U034_NAME]", "Great Dwarven Plague";
  "[RUMOR_U035_DESC]", "Sir Ector was once a Knight of Siria. When his lands were flooded by rain and his family killed by Orcs, he grew depressed. He eventually turned to worship Lord Bane in exchange for many secrets the Dark Lord could teach him.";
  "[RUMOR_U035_NAME]", "Sir Ector";
  "[RUMOR_U036_DESC]", "Although currently at peace for over a decade, the Selentine Empire has often tried to invade Agaria, but it has always been turned back by the Elenian Knights.";
  "[RUMOR_U036_NAME]", "Selentine Empire";
  "[RUMOR_U037_DESC]", "The Trarg is an area south of the Selentine Empire, ruled by tribes of nomadic horsemen.  They often raid the southern reaches of the Empire.  Because they are nomads, they have proven difficult to conquer.";
  "[RUMOR_U037_NAME]", "The Trarg";
  "[RUMOR_U038_DESC]", "Lord Bane and the Agarian Knights have a rivalry extending back many centuries. Every time the Dark Lord has tried to march south, it has been the Agarian Knights (the Sirians in particular) who have held him back and defeated him.";
  "[RUMOR_U038_NAME]", "Conflict with Bane";
  "[RUMOR_U039_DESC]", "Sirian Allfather is the God worshipped by most Agarians.  He is the patron deity of justice, honor and chivalry, protector of the weak, and slayer of evil.  His church is strongest in Siria and Bartonia.";
  "[RUMOR_U039_NAME]", "Sirian Allfather";
  "[RUMOR_U040_DESC]", "House Albion of Siria is one of the oldest noble houses of Agaria.  It's forefathers include the revered King Albion who almost singlehandedly defeated Lord Bane during the Banewars 500 years ago.";
  "[RUMOR_U040_NAME]", "House Albion";
  "[RUMOR_U041_DESC]", "Queen Gwendholyn has ruled over Bartonia for fifteen years.  She has been a wise, kind and noble ruler, and during her reign Bartonia has known unequalled prosperity.";
  "[RUMOR_U041_NAME]", "Queen Gwendholyn";
  "[RUMOR_U042_DESC]", "The people of the Selentine Empire believe their leader is a cruel, untrustworthy and manipulative man, who exploits all those he deals with.";
  "[RUMOR_U042_NAME]", "Emperor Selentius";
  "[RUMOR_U043_DESC]", "Khrona is leader of the Dwarven Merchant's Guild in Dhun-Kor.  She is remarkably well-spoken for a Dwarf, having grown up and been educated in the Selentine Empire, the Borderlands, and Agaria.";
  "[RUMOR_U043_NAME]", "Khrona";
  "[RUMOR_U044_DESC]", "Gruulkar, the current Great Orc, came to power five years ago when he lopped off the previous Great Orc's head in a ritual challenge.  Since then he has been busy trying to organize the local tribes into an effective army.";
  "[RUMOR_U044_NAME]", "Gruulkar";
  "[RUMOR_U045_DESC]", "Lord Sartek was the God of War.  He ruled undisputed over the Realms of War until 500 years ago when he was defeated by his brother Lord Bane, the God of Death.";
  "[RUMOR_U045_NAME]", "Lord Sartek";
  "[RUMOR_U046_DESC]", "The Minotaurs were the greatest creation of the God Sartek.  He called them his favorite children. Their huge size and strength allowed them to capture and control most of the Realms of War.";
  "[RUMOR_U046_NAME]", "Minotaurs";
  "[RUMOR_US00_DESC]", "Creatures from beyond the grave -- Skeletons and Zombies -- have recently been appearing throughout Agaria.  It is all the Knights can do to hold them all back.";
  "[RUMOR_US00_NAME]", "Undead Trouble";
  "[RUMOR_US01_DESC]", "Orc Slavers have been coming over the mountains from Kor, capturing people and hauling them away. This is unusual behavior for Orcs.";
  "[RUMOR_US01_NAME]", "Orc Slavers";
  "[RUMOR_US02_DESC]", "The Dwarves of Dhun-Kor are concerned that too many Orcs are joining forces with Gruulkar.  If their numbers become too great, there may well be an invasion.";
  "[RUMOR_US02_NAME]", "Unrest in Kor";
  "[RUMOR_US03_DESC]", "The Dragons of the Dragonrealm seem to have been taken away. It is believed that the Minotaurs are using some sort of machinery to capture them.";
  "[RUMOR_US03_NAME]", "Missing Dragons";
  "[RUMOR_US04_DESC]", "Lord Sartek, the Dark Horseman of War, was the God of the Minotaurs before Lord Bane carved him up into 101 pieces and distributed him throughout Etheria.";
  "[RUMOR_US04_NAME]", "Lord Sartek";
  "[RUMOR_US05_DESC]", "Lord Bane sent a Minotaur Doomknight -- a huge armored Undead Minotaur -- to occupy the city of Ohtar and bend the Minotaurs to his will.";
  "[RUMOR_US05_NAME]", "Minogoth";
  "[RUMOR_US06_DESC]", "Lord Bane, the Dark Horseman of Death, has ruled the Realms of Death for almost two millenia.  He commands legions of Undead creatures and has a particular hatred of the Agarian Knights.";
  "[RUMOR_US06_NAME]", "Lord Bane";
  "[RUMOR_US07_DESC]", "It seems that Lord Bane has been trading with the Dark Dwarves of Kal-Ungar.  Lord Bane has been paying them with metal from his conquests, and the Dwarves have been working for him.";
  "[RUMOR_US07_NAME]", "Dark Dwarf Trading";
  "[RUNEDUP_HEADING]", "Duplicate Item";
  "[RUNEDUP_TEXT]", "You already have an identical Rune Item to this one. If you create another, you will not receive an extra item. Do you want to continue?";
  "[RUNEKEEPER]", "Runekeeper";
  "[RUNEKEEPER_HELP]", "This opponent is a Runekeeper and guards one of the Runes you can use to create items. As a Runekeeper they possess certain special magic items that allow them to generate extra mana and do extra damage.";
  "[RUNESANDITEMS]", "Runes and Items";
  "[RUNESANDITEMS_HELP]", "You may now use Runes to create magic items here at the Forge. Runes are scattered around the world map and guarded by Runekeepers. To begin, you have been given the 3 most common Runes.";
  "[RUNE_HELP]", "You must defeat this guardian to claim the Rune.";
  "[RUNE_SUCCESS]", "You have added another Rune to your collection.";
  "[RUNE_UAIR_DESC]", "Gives +%d to Yellow Mana at the beginning of each combat.";
  "[RUNE_UAIR_HELP]", "%s of Wind";
  "[RUNE_UAIR_NAME]", "Rune of Air";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_DESC]", "Adds +%d to damage whenever you do 6 or more damage. ";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_NAME]", "Rune of Axes";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_UCHA_NAME]", "Reaver";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_UCRA_NAME]", "Hand Axe";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_UDRA_NAME]", "Dragontooth";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_UDWA_NAME]", "Battle Axe";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_UELV_NAME]", "Francisca";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_UGIA_NAME]", "Cleaver";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_UGOB_NAME]", "Chopper";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_UGOD_NAME]", "Edge";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_UMAG_NAME]", "Tomahawk";
  "[RUNE_UAXE_UMAS_NAME]", "Hatchet";
  "[RUNE_UCAV_DESC]", "Adds +%d%% to Earth Resistance.";
  "[RUNE_UCAV_HELP]", "Deep %s";
  "[RUNE_UCAV_NAME]", "Rune of Caverns";
  "[RUNE_UCHA_DESC]", "Adds -1 to Base Rune ability and adds +150% to Power Rune ability.";
  "[RUNE_UCHA_NAME]", "Rune of Chaos";
  "[RUNE_UCRA_DESC]", "Basic Modifier Rune. No additions to the item.";
  "[RUNE_UCRA_NAME]", "Rune of Crafting";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_DESC]", "Adds +%d to your Morale skill. ";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_NAME]", "Rune of Crowns";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_UCHA_NAME]", "Horns";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_UCRA_NAME]", "Crown";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_UDRA_NAME]", "Crest";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_UDWA_NAME]", "Helm";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_UELV_NAME]", "Circlet";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_UGIA_NAME]", "Greathelm";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_UGOB_NAME]", "Cap";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_UGOD_NAME]", "Halo";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_UMAG_NAME]", "Tiara";
  "[RUNE_UCRN_UMAS_NAME]", "Diadem";
  "[RUNE_UCUN_DESC]", "Adds +%d to your Cunning skill. ";
  "[RUNE_UCUN_NAME]", "Rune of Thought";
